// Pennant Hall, the hub's plaza (plan 41 · EG3; Models/Plaza.cs; docs/data-files.md, "Pennant Hall"). Ours, written by
// hand and read strictly (docs/schemas/plaza.schema.json). The hall ranks by the pennants it has earned ("ranks": what
// each rank asks, the first nothing) and has "pitches" stalls' places at each rank; "places" are the booths' north-west
// tiles in Hub_Plaza (three tiles by three, pitch 1 first), "spots" where the day's guests stand. A guest is a trainer of
// a finished region's table whose class is one of "guestClasses", standing in "guestLooks"' look for the class.
// A stall's words are hubPlaza.stall.<id>.* in ui.json; its service is its keeper's script in Hub_Plaza.txt. A stall opens
// once its "region"'s Hall of Fame is entered (any, with none) and the plaza is at its "rank"; "goods" are what it sells
// for pennants, each from a rank of the plaza on. Later plans add their stalls as rows at the end (plan 41's design).
